cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Kokoro: Mood-conditioned anime and manga retrieval with narrative-arc trajectory matching"
message: "If you use this software or its ideas, please cite it."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Jadhav
    given-names: Gaurav
    email: gauravmakarandjadhav@gmail.com
    alias: JGaurav26
repository-code: "https://github.com/GgauravJ05/kokoro"
url: "https://github.com/GgauravJ05/kokoro"
abstract: >-
  Kokoro learns a continuous affective representation of anime and manga from
  user review text rather than from catalog metadata, using a two-tower
  contrastive retriever trained with InfoNCE and mined hard negatives. The item
  representation is routed through a low-dimensional bottleneck anchored to named
  bipolar mood axes, making every recommendation explainable. Unlike prior work,
  Kokoro models mood as a trajectory over narrative position rather than a single
  point, enabling retrieval on the shape of a work's emotional arc and generating
  calibrated tonal-shift warnings.
keywords:
  - recommender systems
  - information retrieval
  - contrastive learning
  - affective computing
  - dense retrieval
  - interpretability
  - anime
